# Same-document duplicates: one record described twice, both landing on the
# same region page.
#
# These were invisible to the cross-document overlap gate, which only compares
# records from different source files - these come from one. The survivor is
# the more complete record, and it inherits every requirement, effect, region
# link, source and tag the retired copies held, so the merge loses nothing but
# the duplication. Each carried fact names the record it came from.
#
# Deliberately NOT merged: prayers that share a name across two books, and
# training methods listed once per skill they train. Those are told apart by a
# domain scope and merging them would empty a skill list or lose a prayer.
# Official Catalyst task records are left alone.

